From dba0056c0a3c0fd97b9026ebc9850ea4e4196b6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:28:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban backfill: look provenance verdicts up under
 write_txn; prefetch skips foreign refs

creator_chats.backfill warmed the 300 s source cache before write_txn, but a pass that
outlived the TTL reopened every home's state.db per row with the board write lock held.
LinkVerdicts.read now computes is_machine_session for every unreleased chat link and
hub-sub origin (board file and replica) before the transaction, via one prefetch plus
one machine_sessions call per (gateway, profile) (machine_verdicts). resolve_chats /
inherit_chats / _ReplicaReader.resolve take it as `verdicts=` and only look up. A link
that arrives mid-pass is classified without a read when it is another gateway's chat;
a local one fails closed (owns nothing), so its card stays unresolved and the next
pass retries it.

prefetch_sources skips gw/profile/sid refs of other gateways: scoped_sources never
looks them up locally.

Tests (test_kanban_chat_links_bulk_provenance.py): a clock that expires every cache
entry before reuse; at main backfill made 252 provenance reads inside write_txn, now 0.
Batch verdicts equal per-row is_machine_session over the mixed-ref corpus; backfill
output equals the per-row oracle with and without the expiring clock; prefetch of
foreign refs opens no state.db and leaves scoped_sources verdicts unchanged.

Follow-up to #1843 review nits 2 and 3 (t_01a1d2f6289c3fe7).
